  "prefLabel": "Ath 404.01 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ath 404.01 Definitions. \"Sexual misconduct\" means engaging in one or more of the following activities with respect to a current client who is not a spouse or domestic partner:\n\n(a) Engaging in sexual relations, whether consensual or non-consensual;\n\n(b) Making verbal or physical sexual advances;\n\n(c) Using sexual language or phrases;\n\n(d) Requesting sexual favors; or\n\n(e) Engaging in physical contact of a sexual nature.\n\nSource. #9099, eff 3-1-08; ss by #10921, eff 8-29-15; ss by #14247, eff 5-16-25, EXPIRES: 5-16-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ath100-500.html"
